powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "display_name": "Mobile Header",
  "type": 756150001,
  "value": "{% comment %}
  The logo lockup already carries the Ascot Lloyd wordmark, so the site name is
  not repeated beside it. The name is still announced: it is the image's alt
  text, taken from the 'Logo alt text' snippet.

  Dropping the heading also leaves one h1 per page. OT Layout emits
  <h1 class="ot-page__title"> for the page itself, so rendering a second h1
  here gave every page two top-level headings (NFR-ACC-01).
{% endcomment %}
<a href='~/'>
  {% if snippets['Logo URL'] %}<img src='{{ snippets['Logo URL'] }}' alt='{{ snippets['Logo alt text'] }}' style='width: auto; height: 32px; margin: 0 10px;'>{% endif %}
</a>
"
}
